    "concluded": true,
    "explanation": "Across the comparable branches CFH014, CFH017, CFH018 and CFH021, CF-CONFECTIONERY lost 548.5K Units year on year, moving from 4.4M to 3.9M Units and accounting for 176.5% of the total Units decline. The loss was almost entirely concentrated in one product group, CF-CHOCOLATE, which was down 548.1K Units, and within that mainly CHOCOLATE COATED BARS, down 473.5K Units; other declines were much smaller, including CHEWING GUM MINT & MOUTH FRESH at -27.6K, CHOCOLATE BAGS at -26.9K and GIFT PACK CONFECTIONERY at -25.5K, partly offset by small gains in JAR & BAG SWEETS and JAR & BAG CANDIES. By branch, the decline was broad-based but heaviest in CFH021 at -261.8K Units and CFH018 at -155.5K, with smaller losses in CFH014 at -104.1K and CFH017 at -27.1K; transactions also fell in CFH021 and CFH017 but rose slightly in CFH018 and CFH014, so the pattern is associated more with fewer Units per transaction or mix within confectionery than with a universal drop in transactions. Best follow-up check: review the monthly trend for CHOCOLATE COATED BARS by branch, especially CFH021 and CFH018, to see whether the Units loss was concentrated in specific months or tied to a sustained assortment, availability or promotional change.",
