    "explanation": "CFH021 contributed SAR 4.18M of comparable-base Revenue growth, equal to 138.3% of the group’s net change, from SAR 36.76M to SAR 40.94M; the scan already showed this was associated with both higher Units (+128.8K) and higher Transactions (+192.3K), with most of the revenue split sitting in the average value per unit rather than Units alone. The complete item-category drill shows the growth was broad but concentrated in a few categories: CF-MENS FASHION added SAR 805.1K, CF-GROCERY FOOD SAR 580.9K, CF-ELECTRONICS SAR 578.3K, and CF-PERSONAL CARE SAR 521.4K, while CF-FRUIT & VEGETABLES partly offset the gain at -SAR 291.1K. This lines up with the scan’s partial product-group evidence that GM FASHION and FASHION were major contributors, so the likely explanation is that CFH021’s outperformance was associated with a strong mix of fashion-led gains plus support from grocery, electronics and personal care, rather than one isolated category alone. The single best follow-up check is to run a full product_group_name breakdown for CFH021 to verify exactly which product groups roll up into the GM FASHION and FASHION gains and how much each contributed.",
